%N A400294 Numbers that are the difference of positive numbers of the form (k*(k+2))^2 (A099761).
%C A400294 This arises for example in the question whether there might be Pythagorean triples where each of the members is of the form (k+1)^2 - 1, k > 0.
%C A400294 a(41) = A099761(13) - A099761(12) = 9801 = 99^2 = A099761(9) and a(76) = 168^2 = A099761(12) are indeed of this form, corresponding to the triple (10^2 - 1, 13^2 - 1, 14^2 - 1). There is also the larger triple (265^2 - 1, 287^2 - 1, 329^2 - 1), but are there others?
%o A400294 (PARI) A400294_first(n)=my(S=apply(A099761, [1..n])); Set(concat([[S[x]-S[y] | y<-[1..x-1]] |x<-[1..n]]))[1..n]
%Y A400294 Cf. A099761.
%Y A400294 Subsequence of A024352.
